# A grammar that names the same token both as `PLUS` and as `"+"` accepts
# both spellings (or generation fails with a clear error; then turn this
# into a rejection test).
#
# Today: tokenToSymbol maps `.plus` to PLUS only, so every `"+"` alternative
# is silently unreachable: `a + b + c` fails with a ParseError.
# (architecture.md Appendix A: dup.grammar; SPEC §8.3)

@lexer
tokens
    ident
    plus
    eof
    err
'+'                                         → plus
[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*                      → ident
.                                           → err

@parser
@lang = "named_and_literal_terminal"

top! = sum                                  → 1
sum  = IDENT PLUS IDENT                     → (named 1 3)
     | IDENT "+" IDENT "+" IDENT            → (lit 1 3 5)
